---
description: Required Agent Skill routing
alwaysApply: true
---

- Before executing an active Task, read skills/REGISTRY.json.
- Read every SKILL.md listed by the Task required_skills before modifying files.
- A Skill describes method; it never grants write permission beyond Task allowed_write_paths.
- Sprint Planning uses task-planner, but this is owned by the external Planning Agent (ChatGPT), not Cursor execution.
- Cursor MUST NOT invoke task-planner, create/redefine Sprint Tasks, or place task-planner in an active implementation Task required_skills.
- Product implementation uses implementer.
- Adding or changing mapped tests uses test-builder.
- Reproducing/fixing a failure uses debugger.
- Review requires reviewer.
- UI/UX verification requires ui-verifier when the Task touches UI or visual Acceptance.
- Database migration work requires db-migration.
- Release execution follows release-agent and approved release workflows.
- If the active Task needs re-planning, broader write scope, changed AC/Test mapping, or changed commands: STOP, record a Finding, and return to the Planning Agent; do not edit Sprint planning artifacts.
- If a needed Skill is not registered, do not invent a new operating method inside the Task; stop and request governance update.
